;; ============================================================================

;; GLOBAL CODE MOTION  —  port of Simple's `codegen/GlobalCodeMotion.java`
;; ============================================================================
;;
;; ## The problem GCM exists to solve
;;
;; In a sea of nodes a pure node has NO LOCATION. `a*b` floats: it is defined by its inputs and
;; consumed by its users, and nothing says where it executes. GCM is where blocks are invented and
;; every node is assigned to exactly one of them.
;;
;; This is why the IR is worth having. Loop-invariant code motion, common-subexpression
;; elimination and partial-redundancy elimination are not passes here — they are consequences of
;; nodes having floated and then been placed well.
;;
;; ## `buildCFG`, in order
;;
;;     1. reverse post-order over the control subgraph        -> code._cfg
;;     2. schedEarly
;;     3. break up shared global constants by function
;;     4. schedLate
;;
;; The RPO walk skips the Return->CallEnd edge (calls are unwired by this point) and asserts no
;; Call->Fun edge survives. Post-order is built by walking OUTPUTS from Start, then reversed in
;; place.
;;
;; Step 3 is easy to overlook and matters for register allocation: a constant shared by two
;; functions would otherwise be pinned to Start and live across both, so each function gets its own
;; private clone with its own inline-only identity. Constants with no direct function user stay at
;; Start.
;;
;; ## schedEarly — the deepest input wins
;;
;; Walk CFG nodes in RPO. For each, recursively schedule its unpinned, non-CFG inputs FIRST, then:
;;
;;     early = Start                                  ; maximally early, lowest idepth
;;     if in(0) is a CFG node: early = that
;;     for each remaining input: if input.cfg0().idepth() > early.idepth(): early = input.cfg0()
;;     n.setDef(0, early)
;;
;; So a node is placed at its DEEPEST input — the last place all of its operands become available.
;; That is the earliest legal position.
;;
;; The recursion deliberately SKIPS Phi definitions. Simple's comment: because Phis are skipped it
;; "never walks the backedge of Phis (and thus spins around a data-only loop)". A Phi nevertheless
;; exposes its Region immediately through `cfg0()`, before schedEarly visits its arms. Selected Phis
;; do not have that Java virtual query, so we must install the same Region placement before recursing
;; into their inputs. Otherwise backedge arithmetic observes an unplaced Phi and is illegally given
;; Start/Fun as its early bound, allowing the frequency heuristic to hoist it out of the loop.
;;
;; PINNED nodes are not moved at all: Phis, Projs, and anything else that must execute where it was
;; written.
;;
;; ## schedLate — breadth-first, backwards from Stop
;;
;; A node may be placed no later than the LCA (in the dominator tree) of all its uses. Simple walks
;; A sparse worklist starts at Stop and walks definitions backwards. A node becomes ready only when
;; EVERY use already has a placement — you cannot compute an LCA over uses that are not placed yet.
;; When a node finishes, its inputs are pushed because one of their uses just became ready. Loads
;; also wake when any user of their memory definition finishes, because anti-dependence placement
;; waits on those clobbers. A Loop explicitly wakes its Phis to break the loop-carried data cycle.
;; This is final Simple's `breadth`; rescanning the whole arena once per dependency layer turns a
;; deep expression chain into quadratic compile time.
;;
;; Some placements are known immediately rather than computed:
;;
;;     a CFG node   -> itself if a block head, else its cfg(0)
;;     a Phi        -> its Region
;;     a Proj       -> its multi's block
;;
;; Loads additionally wait for their MEMORY input's uses to be placed, because anti-dependences are
;; discovered from those users.
;;
;; ### use_block: a Phi's use is NOT in the Phi's block
;;
;; This is the classic GCM mistake and Simple handles it explicitly. A value feeding arm `i` of a
;; Phi is used on PREDECESSOR `i`, not in the Phi's own block. `use_block` therefore walks the
;; Phi's inputs, and for every arm equal to this node takes the LCA of the matching Region
;; predecessor. Get it wrong and values are pulled into blocks that must not execute them.
;;
;; (A Parm whose Fun matches the node's own function is treated as an ordinary use — the
;; caller-side arm is not this function's business.)
;;
;; ### Choosing between early and late: the frequency heuristic
;;
;; Anywhere on the dominator path from `early` to the use-LCA is legal. Walk UP from the LCA toward
;; early and keep the best:
;;
;;     better(lca, best) =  lca.loopDepth() <  best.loopDepth()   ; shallower loop nesting wins
;;                       || lca is a Never                        ; never hoist past it
;;                       || lca.idepth()    >  best.idepth()      ; else deeper control wins
;;                       || best is an If                         ; never leave it at a block tail
;;
;; Least loop depth FIRST is what makes hoisting out of a loop the default rather than a separate
;; LICM pass. Deepest idepth as the tie-break shortens live ranges, which directly reduces register
;; pressure — GCM's placement choice is the register allocator's input.
;;
;; Before that walk, a singleton-register machine definition scans the late-to-early CFG path for a
;; machine operand constrained to the same register. That CFG use becomes the new early boundary:
;; hoisting above it would manufacture a long fixed-register range that allocation can only spill.
;;
;; ## Anti-dependences: the edges the ideal graph does not carry
;;
;; A Load must be scheduled before any Store that could clobber its alias class, even though no
;; input edge says so. `find_anti_dep` walks LCA->early flagging the Load's candidate blocks, then
;; walks the Load's MEMORY input's users looking for a Store on the SAME ALIAS, and pulls the LCA up
;; to keep the Load above it.
;;
;; This is where the alias classes from `aot.shape` are cashed in: precise classes mean fewer false
;; anti-dependences and therefore more freedom to move loads.
;;
(module aot.codegen.gcm)
(import "coil.alloc" :as alloc)
(import "coil.primitive" :as primitive)
(import "coil.arraylist" :use *)
(import "aot.util.panic" :use *)
(import "aot.node.node" :use *)
(import "aot.node.control" :use *)
(import "aot.node.call" :use *)
(import "aot.node.memory" :use *)
(import "aot.codegen.codegen" :use *)
(import "aot.codegen.machine" :use *)
(import "aot.codegen.regmask" :use *)
(import "aot.codegen.looptree" :use *)
(import "aot.type.type" :use *)

;; The whole pass: RPO, early, break up globals, late.
(defn gcm-build-cfg! [] (-> i64)
  (do
    (gcm-rpo!)
    (gcm-schedule-early!)
    (gcm-break-up-globals!)
    (gcm-schedule-late!)
    0))

(defn gcm-ideal-op [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (match (mach-of n) (Some [m] (m-ideal-op m)) (None [] (n-op n))))

(defn gcm-skip-cfg-edge? [(from (Option (dyn NodeOps))) (to (dyn NodeOps))] (-> bool)
  (match from
    (Some [def]
          (let [from-op (gcm-ideal-op def)
                to-op (gcm-ideal-op to)]
            (if (and (= from-op OP-CALL) (= to-op OP-FUN))
                (do (panic "gcm-rpo!: Call-to-Fun optimizer edge survived unlinking") true)
                (and (= from-op OP-RETURN) (= to-op OP-CALLEND)))))
    (None [] false)))

(defn gcm-rpo-walk! [(from (Option (dyn NodeOps)))
                     (n (dyn NodeOps))
                     (seen (mut (ArrayList bool)))
                     (post (mut (ArrayList i64)))] (-> i64)
  ;; Validate optimizer-only edges before the visited shortcut. A leaked Call->Fun edge normally
  ;; points back to an already-visited Fun; checking `seen` first would silently hide the exact
  ;; unlink failure this guard exists to diagnose.
  (if (or (gcm-skip-cfg-edge? from n)
          (>= (n-nid n) (len (load seen)))
          (get (load seen) (n-nid n))
          (= (n-ty n) TY-XCTRL))
      0
      (match (cfg-of n)
        (None [] 0)
        (Some [_]
              (do
                (set! (mut seen) (n-nid n) true)
                (let [(mut i) 0]
                  (loop (if (>= (load i) (n-nouts n))
                            (break 0)
                            (do
                              (match (n-out n (load i))
                                (Some [use_] (gcm-rpo-walk! (Some n) use_ (mut seen) (mut post)))
                                (None [] 0))
                              (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                              (continue)))))
                (push! [i64] (mut post) (n-nid n))
                0)))))

(defn gcm-block-head [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (match (cfg-of n)
    (Some [cfg]
          (if (block-head? cfg)
              n
              (match (n-in n 0)
                (Some [pred] (gcm-block-head pred))
                (None []
                      (do
                        (panic-i "gcm-block-head: tail has no control predecessor" (n-nid n))
                        (unreachable-node))))))
    (None [] (do (panic-i "gcm-block-head: node is not CFG" (n-nid n)) (unreachable-node)))))

;; Reverse post-order over the control subgraph, into the global CFG list.
(defn gcm-rpo! [] (-> i64)
  (let [a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
        (mut seen) (al-new [bool] a)
        (mut post) (al-new [i64] a)
        limit (+ (arena-node-count) 1)
        (mut i) 0]
    (al-clear! [i64] (mut (.cfg (code))))
    (loop (if (>= (load i) limit)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (push! [bool] (mut seen) false)
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))
    (gcm-rpo-walk! (None [(dyn NodeOps)]) (code-start) (mut seen) (mut post))
    (set! (mut i) (- (len (load post)) 1))
    (loop (if (< (load i) 0)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (push! [i64] (mut (.cfg (code))) (get (load post) (load i)))
                (set! (mut i) (- (load i) 1))
                (continue))))
    (set! (mut i) 0)
    (loop (if (>= (load i) (code-cfg-count))
              (break 0)
              (let [cfg (code-cfg-at (load i))]
                (n-set-block-nid! cfg (n-nid (gcm-block-head cfg)))
                (n-set-early-nid! cfg (n-block-nid cfg))
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))
    (if (= (n-block-nid (code-stop)) 0)
        (panic "gcm-rpo!: selected Stop is unreachable from selected Start")
        (code-cfg-count))))

;; Place every unpinned node at its deepest input.
(defn gcm-node-block [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (let [id (n-block-nid n)]
    (if (= id 0)
        (do (panic-i "gcm-node-block: node has not been placed" (n-nid n)) (unreachable-node))
        (match (arena-node id)
          (Some [block] block)
          (None [] (do (panic-i "gcm-node-block: missing block head" id) (unreachable-node)))))))

(defn gcm-selected-phi? [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> bool)
  (let [op (gcm-ideal-op n)]
    (or (= op OP-PHI) (= op OP-MEMPHI))))

(defn gcm-schedule-early-node! [(n (dyn NodeOps)) (seen (mut (ArrayList bool)))] (-> i64)
  (let [id (n-nid n)]
    (if (or (>= id (len (load seen))) (get (load seen) id))
        0
        (do
          (set! (mut seen) id true)
          ;; Final Simple's `PhiNode.cfg0()` is structurally its Region even before schedEarly has
          ;; visited the Phi. Our selected representation caches cfg0 in `block-nid`; publish that
          ;; fact before following either arm so a loop backedge can use it as an early bound.
          (if (gcm-selected-phi? n)
              (let [region (n-in! n 0)]
                (n-set-block-nid! n (n-block-nid region))
                (n-set-early-nid! n (n-block-nid region)))
              0)
          ;; CFG placement was fixed during RPO. Recurse only through data inputs; following
          ;; control predecessors here would spin around loops and duplicates the RPO walk.
          (let [(mut i) 0]
            (loop (if (>= (load i) (n-nins n))
                      (break 0)
                      (do
                        (match (n-in n (load i))
                          (Some [def]
                                (if (or (cfg? def) (gcm-selected-phi? def))
                                    0
                                    (gcm-schedule-early-node! def (mut seen))))
                          (None [] 0))
                        (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                        (continue)))))
          (if (cfg? n)
              0
              (if (gcm-selected-phi? n)
                  0
                  (if (is-pinned? n)
                      (let [block
                              (match (n-in n 0)
                                (Some [anchor]
                                      (if (= (n-block-nid anchor) 0)
                                          (gcm-node-block (code-start))
                                          (gcm-node-block anchor)))
                                (None [] (gcm-node-block (code-start))))]
                        (n-set-block-nid! n (n-nid block))
                        (n-set-early-nid! n (n-nid block)))
                      (let [(mut early) (gcm-node-block (code-start))
                            (mut j) 0]
                        (loop (if (>= (load j) (n-nins n))
                                  (break 0)
                                  (do
                                    (match (n-in n (load j))
                                      (Some [def]
                                            (if (= (n-block-nid def) 0)
                                                0
                                                (let [candidate (gcm-node-block def)]
                                                  (if (> (cfg-idepth-of candidate)
                                                         (cfg-idepth-of (load early)))
                                                      (set! (mut early) candidate)
                                                      0))))
                                      (None [] 0))
                                    (set! (mut j) (+ (load j) 1))
                                    (continue))))
                        ;; Selected movable nodes reserve input zero for placement. This creates a
                        ;; real def-use edge; list scheduling and late placement consume it.
                        (n-set-def-x! n 0 (Some (load early)))
                        (n-set-block-nid! n (n-nid (load early)))
                        (n-set-early-nid! n (n-nid (load early)))))))
          0))))

(defn gcm-schedule-early! [] (-> i64)
  (let [a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
        (mut seen) (al-new [bool] a)
        limit (+ (arena-node-count) 1)
        (mut i) 0]
    (loop (if (>= (load i) limit)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (push! [bool] (mut seen) false)
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))
    (set! (mut i) 0)
    (loop (if (>= (load i) (code-cfg-count))
              (break 0)
              (let [cfg (code-cfg-at (load i))
                    (mut j) 0]
                (loop (if (>= (load j) (n-nins cfg))
                          (break 0)
                          (do
                            (match (n-in cfg (load j))
                              (Some [def]
                                    (if (cfg? def)
                                        0
                                        (gcm-schedule-early-node! def (mut seen))))
                              (None [] 0))
                            (set! (mut j) (+ (load j) 1))
                            (continue))))
                ;; Phi nodes are outputs of their Region rather than ordinary Region inputs.
                (set! (mut j) 0)
                (loop (if (>= (load j) (n-nouts cfg))
                          (break 0)
                          (do
                            (match (n-out cfg (load j))
                              (Some [use_]
                                    (if (gcm-selected-phi? use_)
                                        (gcm-schedule-early-node! use_ (mut seen))
                                        0))
                              (None [] 0))
                            (set! (mut j) (+ (load j) 1))
                            (continue))))
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))
    0))

;; Give each function its own copy of any constant shared across functions.
(defn gcm-start-pinned-global? [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> bool)
  (and (not (cfg? n))
       (and (> (n-nins n) 0)
            (match (n-in n 0)
              (Some [ctrl]
                    (and (= (gcm-ideal-op ctrl) OP-START)
                         (match (mach-of n)
                           (Some [mach]
                                 (and (m-clone-cheap? mach)
                                      (match (m-outregmap mach) (Some [_] true) (None [] false))))
                           (None [] false))))
              (None [] false)))))

(defn gcm-enclosing-fun [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> (Option (dyn NodeOps)))
  (let [(mut cur) (Some n)
        (mut steps) 0
        limit (+ (arena-node-count) 1)
        (mut answer) (None [(dyn NodeOps)])]
    (loop (if (or (>= (load steps) limit)
                  (match (load cur) (Some [_] false) (None [] true))
                  (match (load answer) (Some [_] true) (None [] false)))
              (break 0)
              (match (load cur)
                (Some [c]
                      (if (= (gcm-ideal-op c) OP-FUN)
                          (set! (mut answer) (Some c))
                          (do
                            (set! (mut cur) (cfg-idom-of c))
                            (set! (mut steps) (+ (load steps) 1))
                            (continue))))
                (None [] (break 0)))))
    (load answer)))

(defn gcm-use-fun [(use_ (dyn NodeOps))] (-> (Option (dyn NodeOps)))
  (if (= (n-block-nid use_) 0)
      (None [(dyn NodeOps)])
      (let [block (gcm-node-block use_)]
        (if (n-same? block (code-start))
            (None [(dyn NodeOps)])
            (gcm-enclosing-fun block)))))

;; Machine clones are born with an input-only copy used by instruction selection. That temporary
;; representation has no matching output edges. Normalize it before installing registered edges,
;; exactly as Simple normalizes both of its possible Node.copy shapes.
(defn gcm-clear-clone-inputs! [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (do
    (if (!= (n-nouts n) 0)
        (broken "gcm-clear-clone-inputs!: fresh clone already has output edges")
        0)
    (loop (if (= (n-nins n) 0)
              (break 0)
              (do (pop! (mut (.ins (hdr n)))) (continue))))
    0))

(defn gcm-clone-input-for-fun [(def_ (dyn NodeOps))
                               (fun (dyn NodeOps))
                               (memo (mut (ArrayList (Option (dyn NodeOps)))))]
                              (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (if (gcm-start-pinned-global? def_)
      (gcm-clone-global-for-fun def_ fun (mut memo))
      def_))

(defn gcm-clone-global-for-fun [(con (dyn NodeOps))
                                (fun (dyn NodeOps))
                                (memo (mut (ArrayList (Option (dyn NodeOps)))))]
                               (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (match (get (load memo) (n-nid con))
    (Some [copy] copy)
    (None []
          (let [copy
                  (match (mach-of con)
                    (Some [mach]
                          (match (m-clone mach)
                            (Some [clone] clone)
                            (None []
                                  (do
                                    (panic-i "gcm-clone-global-for-fun: global is not cloneable"
                                             (n-nid con))
                                    (unreachable-node)))))
                    (None []
                          (do
                            (panic-i "gcm-clone-global-for-fun: global is not a machine node"
                                     (n-nid con))
                            (unreachable-node))))]
            ;; Memoize before following inputs: global materialization chains need cycle safety for
            ;; the same reason as Simple's IdentityHashMap-based recursive clone.
            (set! (mut memo) (n-nid con) (Some copy))
            (gcm-clear-clone-inputs! copy)
            (n-add-def! copy (Some fun))
            ;; This clone is created after schedEarly. Our graph caches Simple's cfg0-derived early
            ;; placement explicitly, so install the same fact that the new control edge represents.
            (n-set-block-nid! copy (n-nid fun))
            (n-set-early-nid! copy (n-nid fun))
            (let [(mut i) 1]
              (loop (if (>= (load i) (n-nins con))
                        (break 0)
                        (do
                          (match (n-in con (load i))
                            (Some [def_]
                                  (n-add-def! copy
                                              (Some (gcm-clone-input-for-fun def_ fun (mut memo)))))
                            (None [] (n-add-def! copy (None [(dyn NodeOps)]))))
                          (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                          (continue)))))
            copy))))

(defn gcm-global-users-splittable? [(con (dyn NodeOps))] (-> bool)
  ;; Final Simple's `breakUpGlobalConstantSingle` returns immediately when an unowned user is not
  ;; another explicitly Start-pinned global. Preserve that result across this separate scan instead
  ;; of merely breaking the loop and then continuing with function reparenting.
  (let [(mut i) 0
        (mut splittable) true]
    (loop (if (or (>= (load i) (n-nouts con)) (not (load splittable)))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (n-out con (load i))
                  (Some [use_]
                        (match (gcm-use-fun use_)
                          (Some [_] 0)
                          (None []
                                (if (gcm-start-pinned-global? use_)
                                    (gcm-break-up-global! use_)
                                    (set! (mut splittable) false)))))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))
    (load splittable)))

(defn gcm-break-up-global! [(con (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (if (not (gcm-global-users-splittable? con))
      0
      (do
        (loop
          (let [(mut fun) (None [(dyn NodeOps)])
                (mut shared) false
                (mut i) 0]
            (loop (if (or (>= (load i) (n-nouts con)) (load shared))
                      (break 0)
                      (do
                        (match (n-out con (load i))
                          (Some [use_]
                                (match (gcm-use-fun use_)
                                  (Some [owner]
                                        (match (load fun)
                                          (Some [first]
                                                (if (n-same? first owner)
                                                    0
                                                    (set! (mut shared) true)))
                                          (None [] (set! (mut fun) (Some owner)))))
                                  (None [] 0)))
                          (None [] 0))
                        (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                        (continue))))
            (match (load fun)
              (None [] (break 0))
              (Some [owner]
                    (if (not (load shared))
                        (do
                          (n-set-def! con 0 (Some owner))
                          (n-set-block-nid! con (n-nid owner))
                          (n-set-early-nid! con (n-nid owner))
                          (break 0))
                        (let [a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
                              (mut memo) (al-new [(Option (dyn NodeOps))] a)
                              limit (+ (arena-node-count) 1)
                              (mut j) 0]
                          (loop (if (>= (load j) limit)
                                    (break 0)
                                    (do
                                      (push! [(Option (dyn NodeOps))]
                                             (mut memo)
                                             (None [(dyn NodeOps)]))
                                      (set! (mut j) (+ (load j) 1))
                                      (continue))))
                          (let [copy (gcm-clone-global-for-fun con owner (mut memo))]
                            (set! (mut j) 0)
                            (loop (if (>= (load j) (n-nouts con))
                                      (break 0)
                                      (match (n-out con (load j))
                                        (Some [use_]
                                              (match (gcm-use-fun use_)
                                                (Some [use-owner]
                                                      (if (n-same? use-owner owner)
                                                          (let [(mut k) 0]
                                                            (loop (if (>= (load k) (n-nins use_))
                                                                      (break 0)
                                                                      (if (n-same? (n-in! use_ (load k)) con)
                                                                          (do
                                                                            (n-set-def! use_
                                                                                        (load k)
                                                                                        (Some copy))
                                                                            (break 0))
                                                                          (do
                                                                            (set! (mut k)
                                                                                  (+ (load k) 1))
                                                                            (continue))))))
                                                          (set! (mut j) (+ (load j) 1))))
                                                (None [] (set! (mut j) (+ (load j) 1)))))
                                        (None [] (set! (mut j) (+ (load j) 1)))))))))))))
        0)))

(defn gcm-break-up-start-globals! [(start (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (let [(mut i) 0]
    (loop (if (>= (load i) (n-nouts start))
              (break 0)
              (match (n-out start (load i))
                (Some [con]
                      (if (gcm-start-pinned-global? con)
                          (let [before (n-nins con)]
                            (gcm-break-up-global! con)
                            (if (or (= (n-nins con) 0)
                                    (not (gcm-start-pinned-global? con))
                                    (!= before (n-nins con)))
                                0
                                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))))
                          (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))))
                (None [] (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))))))
    0))

(defn gcm-break-up-globals! [] (-> i64)
  (let [limit (+ (arena-node-count) 1) (mut nid) 1]
    ;; Simple has one compilation Start. This compiler also has library-declaration Starts whose
    ;; pure constants can remain reachable after their functions are attached to the unit Start.
    ;; Treat every selected Start as the same global-placement boundary.
    (loop (if (>= (load nid) limit)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (arena-node (load nid))
                  (Some [n]
                        (if (= (gcm-ideal-op n) OP-START)
                            (gcm-break-up-start-globals! n)
                            0))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut nid) (+ (load nid) 1))
                (continue))))
    0))

;; Breadth-first backwards from Stop; place each node at the best position between its use-LCA and
;; its early bound.
(defn gcm-selected-reachable? [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> bool)
  (and (!= (n-block-nid n) 0) (or (cfg? n) (mach? n))))

(defn gcm-late-ready? [(n (dyn NodeOps)) (done (mut (ArrayList bool)))] (-> bool)
  (let [(mut i) 0
        (mut ready) true]
    (loop (if (or (>= (load i) (n-nouts n)) (not (load ready)))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (n-out n (load i))
                  (Some [use_]
                        (if (and (gcm-selected-reachable? use_)
                                 (not (get (load done) (n-nid use_))))
                            (set! (mut ready) false)
                            0))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))
    ;; A Load also waits for the users of its memory definition. Stores and calls are not ordinary
    ;; uses of the loaded value, but their chosen blocks determine whether an anti-edge is needed.
    (if (load ready)
        (match (mem-of n)
          (Some [access]
                (if (not (mem-is-load? access))
                    true
                    (let [memory (mem-in access)
                          (mut j) 0]
                      (loop (if (or (>= (load j) (n-nouts memory)) (not (load ready)))
                                (break 0)
                                (do
                                  (match (n-out memory (load j))
                                    (Some [use_]
                                          (if (n-same? use_ n)
                                              0
                                              (let [op (gcm-ideal-op use_)
                                                    clobber
                                                      (match (mem-of use_)
                                                        (Some [other] (not (mem-is-load? other)))
                                                        (None []
                                                              (or (= op OP-CALL)
                                                                  (= op OP-MEMPHI))))]
                                                (if (and clobber
                                                         (and (gcm-selected-reachable? use_)
                                                              (not (get (load done)
                                                                        (n-nid use_)))))
                                                    (set! (mut ready) false)
                                                    0))))
                                    (None [] 0))
                                  (set! (mut j) (+ (load j) 1))
                                  (continue))))
                      (load ready))))
          (None [] true))
        false)))

(defn gcm-late-lca [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> (Option (dyn NodeOps)))
  (let [(mut i) 0
        (mut lca) (None [(dyn NodeOps)])]
    (loop (if (>= (load i) (n-nouts n))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (n-out n (load i))
                  (Some [use_]
                        (if (gcm-selected-reachable? use_)
                            (set! (mut lca)
                                  (idom-lca-nodes (gcm-use-block n use_) (load lca)))
                            0))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))
    (load lca)))

(defn gcm-node-constrains-reg? [(n (dyn NodeOps)) (reg i64)] (-> bool)
  (match (mach-of n)
    (None [] false)
    (Some [mach]
          (let [(mut i) 1
                (mut constrained) false]
            (loop (if (or (>= (load i) (n-nins n)) (load constrained))
                      (break 0)
                      (do
                        (match (m-regmap mach (load i))
                          (Some [mask]
                                (if (mask-test mask reg)
                                    (set! (mut constrained) true)
                                    0))
                          (None [] 0))
                        (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                        (continue))))
            (load constrained)))))

(defn gcm-block-constrains-reg? [(block (dyn NodeOps)) (reg i64)] (-> bool)
  (let [(mut oi) 0
        (mut constrained) (gcm-node-constrains-reg? block reg)]
    ;; Our dominator metadata names block heads, whereas final Simple's chain can name the machine
    ;; CFG tail itself. Inspect the fixed CFG members directly owned by each block so Call/Return/If
    ;; operand constraints form the same hoist boundary.
    (loop (if (or (>= (load oi) (n-nouts block)) (load constrained))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (n-out block (load oi))
                  (Some [use_]
                        (if (and (cfg? use_)
                                 (= (n-block-nid use_) (n-nid block)))
                            (if (gcm-node-constrains-reg? use_ reg)
                                (set! (mut constrained) true)
                                0)
                            0))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut oi) (+ (load oi) 1))
                (continue))))
    (load constrained)))

(defn gcm-constrained-early [(n (dyn NodeOps))
                             (early (dyn NodeOps))
                             (late (dyn NodeOps))] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (match (mach-of n)
    (None [] early)
    (Some [mach]
          (match (m-outregmap mach)
            (None [] early)
            (Some [out]
                  (if (not (mask-singleton? out))
                      early
                      (let [reg (mask-first out)
                            (mut cur-id) (n-nid late)
                            (mut answer-id) (n-nid early)
                            (mut done) false
                            (mut guard) 0]
                        ;; Final Simple stops a singleton-register definition at the first CFG node
                        ;; on late->early whose operand mask admits that same register. Hoisting it
                        ;; above that use would create a long, necessarily conflicting fixed range.
                        (loop (if (load done)
                                  (break 0)
                                  (let [cur
                                          (match (arena-node (load cur-id))
                                            (Some [x] x)
                                            (None [] (unreachable-node)))]
                                    (if (n-same? cur early)
                                        (set! (mut done) true)
                                        (if (gcm-block-constrains-reg? cur reg)
                                            (do
                                              (set! (mut answer-id) (n-nid cur))
                                              (set! (mut done) true))
                                            (match (cfg-idom-of cur)
                                              (Some [parent]
                                                    (set! (mut cur-id)
                                                          (n-nid (gcm-node-block parent))))
                                              (None []
                                                    (do
                                                      (panic "gcm-constrained-early: late is outside early")
                                                      (set! (mut done) true))))))
                                    (set! (mut guard) (+ (load guard) 1))
                                    (if (> (load guard) 1000000)
                                        (broken "gcm-constrained-early: dominator walk did not converge")
                                        0)
                                    (continue))))
                        (match (arena-node (load answer-id))
                          (Some [answer] answer)
                          (None [] (unreachable-node))))))))))

(defn gcm-best-block [(early (dyn NodeOps)) (late0 (dyn NodeOps))] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (let [(mut cur-id) (n-nid late0)
        (mut best-id) (n-nid late0)
        (mut guard) 0]
    (loop (let [cur
                  (match (arena-node (load cur-id))
                    (Some [n] n)
                    (None []
                          (do
                            (panic-i "gcm-best-block: missing dominator block" (load cur-id))
                            (unreachable-node))))]
            (if (n-same? cur early)
                (break 0)
                (if (> (load guard) 1000000)
                    (do (broken "gcm-best-block: dominator walk did not reach early bound") (break 0))
                    (match (cfg-idom-of cur)
                      (Some [parent0]
                            (let [parent (gcm-node-block parent0)
                                  best
                                    (match (arena-node (load best-id))
                                      (Some [n] n)
                                      (None [] (unreachable-node)))]
                              (if (gcm-better? parent best)
                                  (set! (mut best-id) (n-nid parent))
                                  0)
                              (set! (mut cur-id) (n-nid parent))
                              (set! (mut guard) (+ (load guard) 1))
                              (continue)))
                      (None []
                            (do
                              (panic "gcm-best-block: late block is not dominated by early block")
                              (break 0))))))))
    (match (arena-node (load best-id))
      (Some [best] best)
      (None [] (unreachable-node)))))

(defn gcm-place-late! [(n (dyn NodeOps))] (-> i64)
  (let [early
          (match (arena-node (n-early-nid n))
            (Some [block] block)
            (None []
                  (do
                    (panic-i "gcm-place-late!: missing early block" (n-early-nid n))
                    (unreachable-node))))]
    (match (gcm-late-lca n)
      (Some [late]
            (let [bounded
                    (match (mem-of n)
                      (Some [access]
                            (if (mem-is-load? access)
                                (gcm-find-anti-dep late n early)
                                late))
                      (None [] late))
                  constrained-early (gcm-constrained-early n early bounded)
                  best (gcm-best-block constrained-early bounded)]
              (n-set-def! n 0 (Some best))
              (n-set-block-nid! n (n-nid best))))
      ;; A selected value without a selected use is retained only by a keep edge. Its early block
      ;; is the shortest legal lifetime and is already installed.
      (None [] 0))))

(defstruct GcmLateStats [(pushes i64) (pops i64)])

(defn gcm-late-stats [] (-> (ptr GcmLateStats))
  (primitive/alloc-static GcmLateStats))

(defn gcm-last-late-pushes [] (-> i64)
  (.pushes (gcm-late-stats)))

(defn gcm-last-late-pops [] (-> i64)
  (.pops (gcm-late-stats)))

(defn gcm-late-push! [(n (dyn NodeOps))
                      (done (mut (ArrayList bool)))
                      (on (mut (ArrayList bool)))
                      (work (mut (ArrayList i64)))] (-> i64)
  (let [id (n-nid n)]
    (if (or (>= id (len (load done)))
            (get (load done) id)
            (get (load on) id)
            (not (gcm-selected-reachable? n)))
        0
        (do
          (set! (mut on) id true)
          (push! [i64] (mut work) id)
          (set! (.pushes (gcm-late-stats)) (+ (.pushes (gcm-late-stats)) 1))
          1))))

(defn gcm-late-wake-defs! [(n (dyn NodeOps))
                           (done (mut (ArrayList bool)))
                           (on (mut (ArrayList bool)))
                           (work (mut (ArrayList i64)))] (-> i64)
  (let [(mut i) 0]
    (loop (if (>= (load i) (n-nins n))
              (break 0)
              (do
                (match (n-in n (load i))
                  (Some [def]
                        (do
                          (gcm-late-push! def (mut done) (mut on) (mut work))
                          ;; Completing any use of a memory definition may make a waiting Load's
                          ;; anti-dependence layer ready. This is final Simple's def-triggered wakeup.
                          (let [(mut oi) 0]
                            (loop (if (>= (load oi) (n-nouts def))
                                      (break 0)
                                      (do
                                        (match (n-out def (load oi))
                                          (Some [use_]
                                                (match (mem-of use_)
                                                  (Some [access]
                                                        (if (mem-is-load? access)
                                                            (gcm-late-push! use_
                                                                            (mut done)
                                                                            (mut on)
                                                                            (mut work))
                                                            0))
                                                  (None [] 0)))
                                          (None [] 0))
                                        (set! (mut oi) (+ (load oi) 1))
                                        (continue)))))))
                  (None [] 0))
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))
    (if (= (gcm-ideal-op n) OP-LOOP)
        (let [(mut oi) 0]
          (loop (if (>= (load oi) (n-nouts n))
                    (break 0)
                    (do
                      (match (n-out n (load oi))
                        (Some [use_]
                              (if (gcm-selected-phi? use_)
                                  (gcm-late-push! use_ (mut done) (mut on) (mut work))
                                  0))
                        (None [] 0))
                      (set! (mut oi) (+ (load oi) 1))
                      (continue)))))
        0)
    0))

(defn gcm-schedule-late! [] (-> i64)
  (let [a (alloc/malloc-allocator)
        (mut done) (al-new [bool] a)
        (mut on) (al-new [bool] a)
        (mut work) (al-new [i64] a)
        limit (+ (arena-node-count) 1)
        (mut i) 0]
    (loop (if (>= (load i) limit)
              (break 0)
              (do
                (push! [bool] (mut done) false)
                (push! [bool] (mut on) false)
                (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                (continue))))
    (set! (.pushes (gcm-late-stats)) 0)
    (set! (.pops (gcm-late-stats)) 0)
    ;; Final Simple's sparse backwards walk: Stop is the only seed. A completed use wakes its defs;
    ;; a completed memory use additionally wakes Loads sharing that memory definition.
    (gcm-late-push! (code-stop) (mut done) (mut on) (mut work))
    (loop (match (pop! [i64] (mut work))
            (None [] (break 0))
            (Some [id]
                  (do
                    (set! (mut on) id false)
                    (set! (.pops (gcm-late-stats)) (+ (.pops (gcm-late-stats)) 1))
                    (if (get (load done) id)
                        0
                        (match (arena-node id)
                          (Some [n]
                                (if (or (cfg? n)
                                        (is-pinned? n)
                                        (gcm-late-ready? n (mut done)))
                                    (do
                                      (if (or (cfg? n) (is-pinned? n)) 0 (gcm-place-late! n))
                                      (set! (mut done) id true)
                                      (gcm-late-wake-defs! n (mut done) (mut on) (mut work)))
                                    0))
                          (None [] 0)))
                    (continue)))))
    0))

;; The block in which `use_` consumes `n`. For a Phi arm this is the matching Region PREDECESSOR,
;; not the Phi's own block.
(defn gcm-use-block [(n (dyn NodeOps)) (use_ (dyn NodeOps))] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (if (not (gcm-selected-phi? use_))
      (gcm-node-block use_)
      (let [region (n-in! use_ 0)
            (mut found) (None [(dyn NodeOps)])
            (mut i) 1]
        (loop (if (>= (load i) (n-nins use_))
                  (break 0)
                  (do
                    (match (n-in use_ (load i))
                      (Some [arm]
                            (if (n-same? arm n)
                                (match (n-in region (load i))
                                  (Some [pred]
                                        (set! (mut found)
                                              (idom-lca-nodes (gcm-node-block pred) (load found))))
                                  (None []
                                        (panic-i "gcm-use-block: Phi arm has no Region predecessor"
                                                 (load i))))
                                0))
                      (None [] 0))
                    (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                    (continue))))
        (match (load found)
          (Some [block]
                ;; The dominator LCA of sibling projection blocks is their If tail. Instructions
                ;; cannot be left on a tail, so normalize to the tail's containing block now.
                (gcm-node-block block))
          (None []
                (do
                  (panic-i "gcm-use-block: value is not a Phi arm" (n-nid n))
                  (unreachable-node)))))))

;; Least loop depth first, then deepest idepth. Never leaves a node on an If.
(defn gcm-better? [(lca (dyn NodeOps)) (best (dyn NodeOps))] (-> bool)
  (or (< (looptree-depth-of lca) (looptree-depth-of best))
      (= (gcm-ideal-op lca) OP-NEVER)
      (> (cfg-idepth-of lca) (cfg-idepth-of best))
      (= (gcm-ideal-op best) OP-IF)))

;; Pull the LCA up so this Load stays above every Store on the same alias class.
(defn gcm-anti-raise-at [(load_ (dyn NodeOps))
                         (block (dyn NodeOps))
                         (lca (dyn NodeOps))] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (if (!= (n-anti block) (n-nid load_))
      lca
      (match (idom-lca-nodes block (Some lca))
        (Some [x] (gcm-node-block x))
        (None []
              (do
                (panic "gcm-anti-raise-at: conflict has no common dominator")
                (unreachable-node))))))

(defn gcm-anti-raise [(load_ (dyn NodeOps))
                      (conflict (dyn NodeOps))
                      (lca (dyn NodeOps))] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (let [block (gcm-node-block conflict)
        raised (gcm-anti-raise-at load_ block lca)]
    (if (and (n-same? raised block) (not (n-has? (.ins (hdr conflict)) load_)))
        (n-add-def! conflict (Some load_))
        0)
    raised))

(defn gcm-find-anti-dep [(lca (dyn NodeOps)) (load_ (dyn NodeOps)) (early (dyn NodeOps))] (-> (dyn NodeOps))
  (match (mem-of load_)
    (None [] (do (panic "gcm-find-anti-dep: node is not a memory access") (unreachable-node)))
    (Some [load-access]
          (if (not (mem-is-load? load-access))
              (do (panic "gcm-find-anti-dep: memory access is not a Load") (unreachable-node))
              (let [(mut cur-id) (n-nid lca)
                    (mut raised-id) (n-nid lca)
                    (mut done-marking) false
                    (mut guard) 0]
                ;; Candidate blocks are the legal dominator path from use-LCA through early.
                (loop (if (load done-marking)
                          (break 0)
                          (let [cur
                                  (match (arena-node (load cur-id))
                                    (Some [x] x)
                                    (None [] (unreachable-node)))]
                            (n-set-anti! cur (n-nid load_))
                            (if (n-same? cur early)
                                (set! (mut done-marking) true)
                                (match (cfg-idom-of cur)
                                  (Some [parent]
                                        (set! (mut cur-id) (n-nid (gcm-node-block parent))))
                                  (None []
                                        (do
                                          (panic "gcm-find-anti-dep: LCA is outside early bound")
                                          (set! (mut done-marking) true)))))
                            (set! (mut guard) (+ (load guard) 1))
                            (if (> (load guard) 1000000)
                                (broken "gcm-find-anti-dep: dominator marking did not converge")
                                0)
                            (continue))))
                (let [memory (mem-in load-access)
                      (mut i) 0]
                  (loop (if (>= (load i) (n-nouts memory))
                            (break 0)
                            (do
                              (match (n-out memory (load i))
                                (Some [use_]
                                      (if (or (n-same? use_ load_)
                                              (not (gcm-selected-reachable? use_)))
                                          0
                                          (let [op (gcm-ideal-op use_)
                                                conflict
                                                  (match (mem-of use_)
                                                    (Some [other]
                                                          (and (not (mem-is-load? other))
                                                               (= (mem-alias other)
                                                                  (mem-alias load-access))))
                                                    (None [] (= op OP-CALL)))]
                                            (if conflict
                                                (let [current
                                                        (match (arena-node (load raised-id))
                                                          (Some [x] x)
                                                          (None [] (unreachable-node)))
                                                      raised (gcm-anti-raise load_ use_ current)]
                                                  (set! (mut raised-id) (n-nid raised)))
                                                (if (= op OP-MEMPHI)
                                                    (let [region (n-in! use_ 0)
                                                          (mut arm) 1]
                                                      (loop (if (>= (load arm) (n-nins use_))
                                                                (break 0)
                                                                (do
                                                                  (match (n-in use_ (load arm))
                                                                    (Some [state]
                                                                          (if (n-same? state memory)
                                                                              (match (n-in region
                                                                                           (load arm))
                                                                                (Some [pred]
                                                                                      (let [current
                                                                                              (match (arena-node
                                                                                                       (load raised-id))
                                                                                                (Some [x] x)
                                                                                                (None []
                                                                                                      (unreachable-node)))
                                                                                            raised
                                                                                              (gcm-anti-raise-at
                                                                                                load_
                                                                                                (gcm-node-block pred)
                                                                                                current)]
                                                                                        (set! (mut raised-id)
                                                                                              (n-nid raised))))
                                                                                (None []
                                                                                      (panic-i
                                                                                        "gcm-find-anti-dep: MemPhi arm has no predecessor"
                                                                                        (load arm))))
                                                                              0))
                                                                    (None [] 0))
                                                                  (set! (mut arm) (+ (load arm) 1))
                                                                  (continue)))))
                                                    0)))))
                                (None [] 0))
                              (set! (mut i) (+ (load i) 1))
                              (continue)))))
                (match (arena-node (load raised-id))
                  (Some [answer] answer)
                  (None [] (unreachable-node))))))))
